  "question": {
    "text": "If the velocity of light in vacuum is $3 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}$, the time taken (in nanosecond) to travel through a glass plate of thickness $10 \\mathrm{cm}$ and refractive index 1.5 is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "0.5",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "3",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $v=3 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}, d=10 \\mathrm{m}$ and $\\mu=1.5$\r\nHere, $t=\\frac{d}{c / \\mu}$\r\n$$\r\nt=\\frac{10 \\times 10^{-2}}{2 \\times 10^{8}}\r\n$$\r\n$\\left(\\therefore \\frac{c}{\\mu}=\\frac{3 \\times 10^{8}}{1.5}=2 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{ms}^{-1}\\right)$\r\n$t=0.5 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{s}$"
  }
}